Criteria
--------
(judgment calls, not values from any source)
charging: on AC power, macOS's charging flag on and the battery current above 50 mA;
         stopped: on AC power, the flag off and the current from -99 to 50 mA;
         discharging: the flag off and the current -100 mA or lower; anything else disagrees
sustained: 5 readings in a row, each at least 1.5 s after the previous counted one,
           spanning at least 8.0 s, of at least 2 battery updates (UpdateTime values);
           closer readings are not counted, a contradicting one breaks the run; an update counts as
           made after a moment only if its UpdateTime is in a later second
effect: a sustained stop or discharge beginning within 90.0 s of creation, from an update made
           after it, every reading after it the same until the release; the release accepted and
           no longer listed; then a sustained resume beginning within 120.0 s of the release
adapter cut: every discharging reading reports the adapter attached and a system power input of
           at most 1000 mW; otherwise discharging with adapter attached, or inconclusive
no effect: every reading while held charging, of at least 2 updates made after creation
did not resume: no charging reading in at least 120.0 s after the release, over at least
           2 updates made after it
baseline: at least 20 s and 2 updates, at most 150 s, all charging; its latest
           update at most 70.0 s old at creation
inconclusive: 100% or charged, unreadable, a battery update older than 150.0 s or a charge
           below 25% while held, a failed or unconfirmed release, a sleep notification, a gap over
           10.0 s between readings, or clocks that disagree by more than 2.0 s

Verdict: adapter cut
--------------------
The Mac ran from its battery from 4.0 s after the assertion was created until
it was released, and charging resumed 6.0 s after a confirmed release (each
over 5 readings at least 1.5 s apart, spanning at least 8.0 s, of at least 2
battery updates). Adapter power was back 6.0 s after the release. That the
adapter's power was cut is inferred [INFERRED/UNVERIFIED]: the battery
discharged while every reading still reported the adapter attached and a
system power input of at most 1000 mW, from after the creation until the
release. On this Mac, macOS build and firmware, the DisableInflow assertion
then cuts the adapter's power, and releasing it restores it. Confirm that the
adapter stayed plugged in.

